1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,333
Where are you going?

2
00:00:02,633 --> 00:00:03,899
I'm late! I'm late!

3
00:00:04,199 --> 00:00:06,465
Oh dear, oh dear, what shall I do?

4
00:00:06,765 --> 00:00:07,965
Come back here!

5
00:00:08,265 --> 00:00:09,598
Wait for me, please.

6
00:00:09,898 --> 00:00:11,098
Who are you?

7
00:00:11,398 --> 00:00:12,598
I don't know.

8
00:00:12,898 --> 00:00:14,298
Have you seen my cat?

9
00:00:14,598 --> 00:00:16,731
She's very small and very white.

10
00:00:17,031 --> 00:00:18,231
Don't be afraid.

11
00:00:18,531 --> 00:00:19,997
Open the door, please.

12
00:00:20,297 --> 00:00:21,763
The door is too small.

13
00:00:22,063 --> 00:00:23,396
I can't get through.

14
00:00:23,696 --> 00:00:24,896
Drink this.

15
00:00:25,196 --> 00:00:26,396
Now I'm too big!

16
00:00:26,696 --> 00:00:27,896
Now I'm too small.

17
00:00:28,196 --> 00:00:29,729
Where did everybody go?

18
00:00:30,029 --> 00:00:31,495
What a strange garden.

19
00:00:31,795 --> 00:00:33,061
Flowers can't talk.

20
00:00:33,361 --> 00:00:34,827
Of course we can talk.

21
00:00:35,127 --> 00:00:36,327
Sing us a song.

22
00:00:36,627 --> 00:00:38,160
I don't know any songs.

23
00:00:38,460 --> 00:00:39,660
Then go away.

24
00:00:39,960 --> 00:00:41,360
You're all very rude.

25
00:00:41,660 --> 00:00:42,993
The queen is coming!

26
00:00:43,293 --> 00:00:44,493
Everyone bow!

27
00:00:44,793 --> 00:00:45,993
Off with his head!

28
00:00:46,293 --> 00:00:48,093
She is the Queen of Hearts.

29
00:00:48,393 --> 00:00:49,593
Do you play cards?

30
00:00:49,893 --> 00:00:51,559
I've never played before.

31
00:00:51,859 --> 00:00:53,059
Give me the ball.

32
00:00:53,359 --> 00:00:54,559
Where is the ball?

33
00:00:54,859 --> 00:00:56,059
It ran away.

34
00:00:56,359 --> 00:00:57,559
Balls don't run.

35
00:00:57,859 --> 00:00:59,059
This one does.

36
00:00:59,359 --> 00:01:00,559
Have some tea.

37
00:01:00,859 --> 00:01:02,192
There isn't any tea.

38
00:01:02,492 --> 00:01:03,825
Then have some cake.

39
00:01:04,125 --> 00:01:05,325
I don't want cake.

40
00:01:05,625 --> 00:01:06,825
What time is it?

41
00:01:07,125 --> 00:01:09,058
It's always six o'clock here.

42
00:01:09,358 --> 00:01:11,291
Why is it always six o'clock?

43
00:01:11,591 --> 00:01:13,457
Because the clock is broken.

44
00:01:13,757 --> 00:01:15,090
Who broke the clock?

45
00:01:15,390 --> 00:01:16,590
Nobody knows.

46
00:01:16,890 --> 00:01:18,823
Sit down and tell me a story.

47
00:01:19,123 --> 00:01:21,856
Once upon a time there was a little girl.

48
00:01:22,156 --> 00:01:23,889
She fell into a deep hole.

49
00:01:24,189 --> 00:01:26,255
At the bottom she found a door.

50
00:01:26,555 --> 00:01:28,488
Behind the door was a garden.

51
00:01:28,788 --> 00:01:30,521
In the garden lived a cat.

52
00:01:30,821 --> 00:01:32,154
The cat could smile.

53
00:01:32,454 --> 00:01:33,654
Can cats smile?

54
00:01:33,954 --> 00:01:35,154
This one can.

55
00:01:35,454 --> 00:01:36,920
Which way should I go?

56
00:01:37,220 --> 00:01:39,686
That depends on where you want to go.

57
00:01:39,986 --> 00:01:41,586
I don't much care where.

58
00:01:41,886 --> 00:01:44,552
Then it doesn't matter which way you go.

59
00:01:44,852 --> 00:01:46,252
Everyone here is mad.

60
00:01:46,552 --> 00:01:47,752
Am I mad?

61
00:01:48,052 --> 00:01:50,518
You must be, or you wouldn't be here.

62
00:01:50,818 --> 00:01:52,751
Good afternoon, Your Majesty.

63
00:01:53,051 --> 00:01:55,117
Why are you painting the roses?

64
00:01:55,417 --> 00:01:57,683
We planted white roses by mistake.

65
00:01:57,983 --> 00:01:59,716
The queen wanted red ones.

66
00:02:00,016 --> 00:02:03,349
If she sees white roses, she'll cut off our heads.

67
00:02:03,649 --> 00:02:04,849
Help us, please!

68
00:02:05,149 --> 00:02:06,615
Pass me the red paint.

69
00:02:06,915 --> 00:02:08,115
Here you are.

70
00:02:08,415 --> 00:02:09,748
Thank you very much.

71
00:02:10,048 --> 00:02:11,248
You're welcome.

72
00:02:11,548 --> 00:02:13,348
Let's run before she comes.

73
00:02:13,648 --> 00:02:15,114
Too late. Here she is.

74
00:02:15,414 --> 00:02:17,080
What is your name, child?

75
00:02:17,380 --> 00:02:19,446
My name is Alice, Your Majesty.

76
00:02:19,746 --> 00:02:21,346
Do you know how to play?

77
00:02:21,646 --> 00:02:22,846
A little.

78
00:02:23,146 --> 00:02:24,346
Then play!

79
00:02:24,646 --> 00:02:25,912
This is impossible.

80
00:02:26,212 --> 00:02:27,945
Only if you believe it is.

81
00:02:28,245 --> 00:02:31,511
I believe six impossible things before breakfast.

82
00:02:31,811 --> 00:02:33,811
How many brothers do you have?

83
00:02:34,111 --> 00:02:36,444
I have two brothers and one sister.

84
00:02:36,744 --> 00:02:38,210
My father is a farmer.

85
00:02:38,510 --> 00:02:40,310
My mother teaches children.

86
00:02:40,610 --> 00:02:43,276
We live in a small house near the river.

87
00:02:43,576 --> 00:02:45,642
Every morning I walk to school.

88
00:02:45,942 --> 00:02:47,808
Today the teacher was angry.

89
00:02:48,108 --> 00:02:50,041
Nobody had done the homework.

90
00:02:50,341 --> 00:02:53,074
Tomorrow we will write a letter in Latin.

91
00:02:53,374 --> 00:02:55,507
Can you help me with the letter?

92
00:02:55,807 --> 00:02:57,007
Yes, gladly.

93
00:02:57,307 --> 00:02:58,773
First write your name.

94
00:02:59,073 --> 00:03:00,406
Then write the date.

95
00:03:00,706 --> 00:03:02,106
What day is it today?

96
00:03:02,406 --> 00:03:03,606
It's Tuesday.

97
00:03:03,906 --> 00:03:05,506
I thought it was Monday.

98
00:03:05,806 --> 00:03:07,006
You were wrong.

99
00:03:07,306 --> 00:03:08,506
I'm never wrong.

100
00:03:08,806 --> 00:03:10,672
Everyone is wrong sometimes.

101
00:03:10,972 --> 00:03:12,172
Look at the sky!

102
00:03:12,472 --> 00:03:13,738
It's going to rain.

103
00:03:14,038 --> 00:03:15,238
Let's go inside.

104
00:03:15,538 --> 00:03:16,738
Close the window.

105
00:03:17,038 --> 00:03:18,238
Light the candle.

106
00:03:18,538 --> 00:03:19,738
It's dark in here.

107
00:03:20,038 --> 00:03:21,838
Are you afraid of the dark?

108
00:03:22,138 --> 00:03:23,338
Not at all.

109
00:03:23,638 --> 00:03:25,304
Then why are you shaking?

110
00:03:25,604 --> 00:03:26,804
I'm cold.

111
00:03:27,104 --> 00:03:28,304
Take my coat.

112
00:03:28,604 --> 00:03:29,804
You are very kind.

113
00:03:30,104 --> 00:03:31,637
Good night, sleep well.

114
00:03:31,937 --> 00:03:33,137
See you tomorrow.
